<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above Un-Audited standalone financial results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board at their respective meeting held on 24th Feburary, 2021.  n tttttt   n2. As there are no operations in the holding and subsidiary company, segment reporting is not prepared and not required to be submitted.  n tttttt   n3. The figures for the previous period have been regrouped/reclassified wherever necessary.t   n tttttt   n4. As on 30th September 2020, there is no pending litigation of the Holding company. Also there is no pending litigation of subsidiary company except in respect of disputed statutory dues of MVAT and KVAT.  n  n tttttt   n5. During this quarter Remuneration to Managing Director has been waived.ttttt   n tttttt   n6. The Holding Company had executed an agreement with KKN Holdings Private Limited (Formerly known as Foundation outsourcing India Private Limited) for purchase of 4,00,000 equity shares of Artmatrix Technology Sdn Bhd for Rs, 260 crores. However, this transaction could not be completed because the shares of Artmatrix SDN BHD are recognised by a Unique Identification Number (UIN) allotted by RBI, which is still in the name of Vector Projects India Pvt. Ltd. The Holding Company has been advised to defer the transfer of shares until the UIN Number is transferred to KKN Holdings Pvt Ltd. In terms of renewed agreement, the underlying shares should be transferred to the Company on or before 31st December 2021. The Holding company has already advanced Rs 260 crores to KKN Holdings Private Limited (KKNHPL).   n tttttt   n7. The Holding Company had given various advances to KKN Holdings Private Limited (Formerly known as Foundation Outsourcing Private Limited) outstanding balance of which was Rs.204.37 crores as on 01.07.2020. The management of the Holding Company believes that underlying assets shall be transferred to the Company and capitalised by 31.03.2021 and / or surplus / deficit, if any, shall be repaid back to / paid by the Company. Few extracts of advance to KKN have been provided hereinbelow:  n  na) The Holding Company had Inter Corporate Deposits with Vector Projects India Private Limited (‘VPIPL’), wholly owned subsidiary company, amounting to Rs. 36,60,37,884/- during earlier years. During the financial year 2019-20, these Inter Corporate Deposits have been adjusted and treated as advance to KKNHPL with mutual consent from both the parties.  n  nb) The Holding Company had Inter Corporate Deposits with Super Band Private Limited (having common directors Mr. Keshav Narayan Kantamneni and Ramgopal Lakshmi Ratan) amounting of 45,89,88,012/- during earlier years. During the financial year 2019-20, these Inter Corporate Deposits have been adjusted and treated as advance to KKNHPL with mutual consent from both the parties.   n  nc) The Holding company had given advance for purchase of shares amounting to Rs. 6,00,00,000/- to two shareholders of AT Broadband Private Limited for purchase of 20,000 shares of AT Broadband Private Limited. Underlying agreement was cancelled during the year the sum of Rs. 120000000 has been treated as advance to KKNHPL.  n  nDuring the quarter under review, KKN repaid Rs. 5.95 crores by way of certain payments to Creditors of the Company (related parties) by virtue of this balance of advance to KKN has been reduced to Rs.198.42 crores as at 30.09.2020. Extracts for major payments are provided hereinbelow:  n  n(i) Payment to Vector Projects India Private Limited of Rs. 3.17 crores.  n(ii) Payment to Uniply Decor Limited of Rs. 2.37 crores.  n  nComplete notes can't be provided here since only 4000 characters here since only 4000 charactes will accommodate. For complete notes quick results can be viewed</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
